---
description: Nil/empty guards only with documented evidence; explain each keep
globs: "**/*.go"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Evidence-based nil and empty checks

Do not add `== nil`, `== ""`, `IsZero`, or `== 0` guards “just in case.”

Add such a check **only** when you know the value can be absent — from API/docs, generated types (`omitempty` pointers), observed payloads, or an explicit product/proto absence rule. If evidence is missing, omit the guard; prefer a clear panic over speculative soft-skips.

Every kept guard gets a short comment stating **why** absence is real (cite the source of truth in a few words).

```go
// BAD — no evidence YouTube omits requested snippet
if item.Snippet == nil {
	continue
}

// BAD — silent skip with no comment
if id == "" {
	return
}

// GOOD — proto/domain absence (conventional API response)
// Leave Duration unset: unknown/zero must not become a zero protobuf Duration.
if video.Duration > 0 {
	msg.Duration = durationpb.New(video.Duration)
}

// GOOD — documented API quirk
// YouTube omits likeCount (or returns 0) when ratings are hidden.
if item.Statistics.LikeCount == 0 {
	return details
}
```

## Not this rule

- `err != nil` and other real error handling
- Pal-injected collaborator nil checks — never; see `pal-components` (nil means wiring is broken)
- Auth/config fail-fast empties that are already product requirements (`DatabaseURL`, OAuth `code`) — still comment if non-obvious
- Generated code (`ent/`, protos, mocks)
